<entry key="OpenBikeCAD.material">Mild / high-tensile ERW steel, fillet brazed (bronze)</entry>
<entry key="OpenBikeCAD.drawingDate"></entry>
<entry key="OpenBikeCAD.notes">20 inch (ISO 406, Brompton G Line size) twin straight-tube step-through, one size for riders ~150-190 cm. 54-406 tyres on 406 x 22 rims (ERD ~392, check). 390 mm head tube puts the bars where the 700c bike has them. Upper tube meets the seat tube 150 mm above BB. Wishbone seatstays; chainstays dimpled 7 mm. Horizontal dropouts, 132 mm OLD, Shimano Nexus 7/8, 42/16. Seatpost 30.9 x 400. Brakes: V-brake front (posts ~80 c-c, 177 mm from axle), Nexus roller brake rear (reaction arm clip on left chainstay). Braze-ons: fender eyelets, rack mounts for an adult passenger, chainguard tabs, kickstand plate, ring-lock bosses, bottle mount. Carrier-block mounting block brazed LOW: centre 60 mm above the head tube bottom, so a bag up to ~495 mm tall fits under the bars (~330 mm at the standard position). Motor-ready fork: 310 A-C, 32 rake, 6 mm dropouts, 10 mm slots, torque arm, 3 cable guides.</entry>
